---
source: crates/chain-syntax/tests/it/bad.rs
expression: "annotate(&text, &parsed.diagnostics)"
---
  1 | chain 1
  2 | compressor #1 key=@3
    |               ^ 2:15: error E210: `@3` comes later in the signal: a node can only listen to a node before it
  3 | compressor #2 key=@2
    |               ^ 3:15: error E210: `@2` is the node itself: a node cannot listen to its own output
  4 | compressor #3 key=@9
    |               ^ 4:15: error E210: no node of this chain has the id `#9`
  5 | eq #4
    | ^ 5:1: error E209: `eq` is a device, so it holds no nodes; only a split does
  6 |   compressor #5
  7 | band #6 xover=2kHz,150Hz
    | ^ 7:1: error E208: a `band` split takes 2 to 6 branches; this one has 1
    |         ^ 7:9: error E212: the values of `xover` must go up: `2kHz,150Hz`
  8 |   | Low
  9 | band #7 xover=1kHz
 10 |   | Low
 11 |   | Mid
 12 |   | High
 13 |   mods
 14 |     lfo #8 -> #1.threshold -3dB
    |               ^ 14:15: error E211: `#1` is not a node or a branch in this container
 15 | rack #10
 16 |   saturation #11
 17 |   mods
 18 |     macro #12 -> #11.drve +3dB, #11.curve +1, #11.drive +3Hz
    |                  ^ 18:18: error E211: `#11` has no parameter `drve`; did you mean `drive`?
    |                                 ^ 18:33: error E211: `curve` is not a number, so it cannot be modulated
    |                                               ^ 18:47: error E204: a depth on `drive` is a number in dB or in %, not `3Hz`
 19 |     wobble #13
    |     ^ 19:5: error E201: no modulator `wobble`
